From b879a4b3de8ada95c9be8181eafbb163329a43a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:18:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: power down a device whose firmware is still
 booting

ath12k_pci_power_down() returns early unless ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE
is set, so that a device a partner in its hardware group already powered
down is skipped. But ath12k_pci_power_up() clears that flag, and only
ath12k_pci_start() sets it again, once the firmware is ready. A device
removed while its firmware boots, at probe or during recovery, is
therefore never powered down: MHI stays up, and its channel devices
outlive the controller that mhi_unregister_controller() frees.

On a WCN7860 removed in the middle of a recovery, the next probe found
the old mhi0_IPCR still registered, and its first QMI request went out
through the stale QRTR endpoint:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffff80009b9cee08
  Workqueue: ath12k_qmi_driver_event ath12k_qmi_driver_event_work [ath12k]
  pc : mhi_queue+0x34/0x184
  Call trace:
   mhi_queue+0x34/0x184 (P)
   mhi_queue_skb+0x4c/0x7c
   qcom_mhi_qrtr_send+0x64/0x150
   ...
   ath12k_qmi_phy_cap_send+0x78/0x19c [ath12k]
   ath12k_qmi_event_server_arrive+0x50/0x2d0 [ath12k]
  sysfs: cannot create duplicate filename '/bus/mhi/devices/mhi0_IPCR'

Track the power state itself: set a flag in ath12k_pci_power_up() and
let only the first ath12k_pci_power_down() after it act.

Fixes: dce7aec6b1f7 ("wifi: ath12k: fix failed to set mhi state error during reboot with hardware grouping")
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c | 7 ++++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 4270f5d6c..1cbc55aeb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1452,6 +1452,7 @@ int ath12k_pci_power_up(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 
 	ab_pci->register_window = 0;
 	clear_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags);
+	set_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_POWERED_UP, &ab_pci->flags);
 	ath12k_pci_sw_reset(ab_pci->ab, true);
 
 	/* Disable ASPM during firmware download due to problems switching
@@ -1480,7 +1481,11 @@ void ath12k_pci_power_down(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
 
-	if (!test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags))
+	/* A partner device of the group may have powered this one down
+	 * already. INIT_DONE can't tell: it stays clear until the firmware
+	 * is ready, while MHI is already up.
+	 */
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_POWERED_UP, &ab_pci->flags))
 		return;
 
 	/* restore aspm in case firmware bootup fails */
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.h
index 0e0e2020c..bd425bf75 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.h
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@ enum ath12k_pci_flags {
 	ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_IS_MSI_64,
 	ATH12K_PCI_ASPM_RESTORE,
 	ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_MULTI_MSI_VECTORS,
+	ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_POWERED_UP,
 };
 
 struct ath12k_pci_ops {
-- 
